  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 16—Certification trade marks",
    "16.2  Documents to be sent to Commission"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "16.2",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r16.2",
  "text": "(1) If, after examining an application, the Registrar is satisfied that: (a) the application has been made in accordance with this Act; and (b) there are no grounds for rejecting it; the Registrar must send to the Commission copies of the documents mentioned in subregulation (2). (2) For subregulation (1), the documents are: (a) the application for registration; and (b) a notification of any amendment made to the application for registration of a certification trade mark; and (c) a copy of the rules governing the use of the certification trade mark; and (d) any other document that is relevant to the application.",
